{"name":"Guacamole Ambrosia","hex":"#d2d392","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"guacamole","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An avocado-based greenish dip with onions, tomato, and spices, common to Mexican cuisine and often served with tortilla chips."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guacamole"},{"term":"ambrosia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The food of the gods, thought to confer immortality.","The anointing-oil of the gods."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambrosia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Guacamole","blocks":[{"text":"Guacamole, sometimes informally shortened to guac in the United States, is an avocado-based dip, spread, or salad first developed in Mexico. In addition to its use in modern Mexican cuisine, it has become part of international cuisine as a dip, condiment, and salad ingredient."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Guacamole_IMGP1271.jpg/330px-Guacamole_IMGP1271.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guacamole","wikidata":"Q207968"},{"title":"Ambrosia","blocks":[{"text":"In the ancient Greek myths, ambrosia is the food or drink of the Greek gods, and is often depicted as conferring longevity or immortality upon whoever consumed it. It was brought to the gods in Olympus by doves and served either by Hebe or by Ganymede at the heavenly feast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/WLANL_-_MicheleLovesArt_-_Museum_Boijmans_Van_Beuningen_-_Istoriato_schotel%2C_de_maaltijd_der_Goden_op_de_Olympus.jpg/330px-WLANL_-_MicheleLovesArt_-_Museum_Boijmans_Van_Beuningen_-_Istoriato_schotel%2C_de_maaltijd_der_Goden_op_de_Olympus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambrosia","wikidata":"Q131409"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Guacomole.jpg/500px-Guacomole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Guacomole.jpg/1280px-Guacomole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Guacomole.jpg/500px-Guacomole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Guacamole with tortilla chips","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuacomole.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Guasacaca_avocado_sauce-1500x1000.jpg/500px-Guasacaca_avocado_sauce-1500x1000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Guasacaca_avocado_sauce-1500x1000.jpg/1280px-Guasacaca_avocado_sauce-1500x1000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Guasacaca_avocado_sauce-1500x1000.jpg/500px-Guasacaca_avocado_sauce-1500x1000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Guasacaca in a mason jar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuasacaca_avocado_sauce-1500x1000.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Johann_Balthasar_Probst_002.jpg/330px-Johann_Balthasar_Probst_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Johann_Balthasar_Probst_002.jpg/330px-Johann_Balthasar_Probst_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thetis anoints Achilles with ambrosia, by Johann Balthasar Probst (1673–1748)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohann_Balthasar_Probst_002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Mosaik_%22Wahnsinn_des_Lykurg%22_%E2%80